# Architectural boundary rules — enforced by .claude/hooks/boundary-check.sh
# on every edit, and swept by /validate-phase and /refresh-index.
#
# Syntax (one directive per line, # comments allowed):
#   layer <name> <dir-prefix>/     declares a layer as a directory prefix
#   deny <from> -> <to>            files under <from> may not import from <to>
#
# Only encode edges the codebase actually respects (or has decided to adopt via
# ADR). A rule the code already violates makes the hook cry wolf on every edit.
#
# The engine edge ("simulation must not touch UnityEngine / Godot / Unreal") is
# NOT expressible here — layers are repo directory prefixes and the engine is
# not a directory in the repo. Enforce it with the build system instead, which
# catches fully-qualified names and transitive deps that grep cannot:
#   Unity:  asmdef on the sim dir with "noEngineReferences": true
#   Godot:  a domain .csproj that does not reference Godot.NET.Sdk
#   Unreal: a sim module whose Build.cs does not depend on Engine
# Changing this file requires an ADR — the prose twin of these rules lives in
# docs/constraints.md §Layering.
#
# Example (taskboard: routes → services → db, no skipping, no upward imports):

layer routes src/routes/
layer services src/services/
layer db src/db/

deny routes -> db
deny services -> routes
deny db -> services
deny db -> routes
